<Slide notes={`Four things for the next person. Write the target claim down before the first paid call. Isolate the ablation cache before running anything. Print the metric edges next to the first result. Report distributions, not points. And the k=40 pass: nine points of overall gap were my setting; sixteen to thirty-four on multi-hop and open-domain were not. A reproduction that measures one setting cannot tell those apart.`} style={{ padding: 0, background: '#FFFFFF', fontFamily: 'Arial' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: 1280, height: 64, background: '#1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', marginLeft: 60 }}>Advice — and the number that matters</Text>
    <Text style={{ color: '#B8C7E6', fontSize: 16, marginLeft: 'auto', marginRight: 60 }}>FTEC5660 · Reproducibility</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 676, left: 60, width: 1160, height: 20, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between', alignItems: 'center' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#8B97A8', fontSize: 14 }}>Reproducing A-MEM on LoCoMo</Text>
    <Text style={{ color: '#8B97A8', fontSize: 14 }}>15 / 16</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 64, left: 60, width: 1160, height: 606, flexDirection: 'column', paddingTop: 34, paddingBottom: 40 }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#1E4FA8', fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 1, marginBottom: 16 }}>ADVICE TO THE NEXT PERSON</Text>
    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #E5E7EB' }}>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1E4FA8', fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', width: 60 }}>01</Text>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1A2230', fontSize: 20, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>Write the target claim down before the first paid call.</Text>
    </Box>
    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #E5E7EB' }}>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1E4FA8', fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', width: 60 }}>02</Text>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1A2230', fontSize: 20, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>Isolate the ablation cache before running anything — this is the failure that fakes a null result.</Text>
    </Box>
    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #E5E7EB' }}>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1E4FA8', fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', width: 60 }}>03</Text>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1A2230', fontSize: 20, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>Print the metric edges next to the first result — a swallowed exception reads as a low score.</Text>
    </Box>
    <Box style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingTop: 16, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #E5E7EB' }}>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1E4FA8', fontSize: 20, fontWeight: 'bold', width: 60 }}>04</Text>
      <Text style={{ color: '#1A2230', fontSize: 20, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>Report distributions, not points — the zero BLEU column was only visible across three trials.</Text>
    </Box>
    <Box style={{ background: '#1E4FA8', paddingTop: 22, paddingBottom: 22, paddingLeft: 26, paddingRight: 26, marginTop: 28, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 28 }}>
      <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 44, fontWeight: 'bold', lineHeight: 1 }}>9 vs 16–34</Text>
      <Text style={{ color: '#E8EFF8', fontSize: 20, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>points of the overall gap were my setting; the multi-hop and open-domain deficits were not. A reproduction that measures one setting cannot tell those apart.</Text>
    </Box>
  </Box>
</Slide>
